\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 VHSart \'97 Monochrome Horizontal Static & Luma Streaks\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Objective\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated VHSart preset that reconstructs the supplied reference video, 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mov
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  (~1.006 seconds).\
The effect consists of dense, full-frame monochrome horizontal static that evolves over time. Its defining characteristic is a temporal transition: the first frames contain dense fine-grained noise and short horizontal segments, while the final observed frame develops longer, smoother horizontal streaks and luminance smearing.\
The result must be entirely procedural inside the native C++ After Effects plugin. Do not use pre-rendered textures, stock footage, images, GIFs, or external overlays.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Important:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  The Adobe Stock watermark visible in the reference is not part of the effect and must never be recreated.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Inspect Existing VHSart Engines Before Implementation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Thoroughly inspect the existing project and identify the available:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Static and signal-noise generators.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Monochrome and luminance-noise processing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal noise and scanline systems.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal smear and streak processing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dropout generation.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal modulation and seed systems.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Input blending and alpha compositing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Prefer a dedicated preset configured through existing VHSart engines.\
Do not create a duplicate noise engine unnecessarily. If the existing engines lack precise horizontal streak modulation or the required temporal transition, extend the appropriate existing engine with dedicated controls.\
Preserve all existing presets, effects, and functionality.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Primary Component \'97 Full-Frame Monochrome Horizontal Static\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Generate dense monochrome static across 100% of the frame.\
Visual requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Black, dark gray, medium gray, light gray, and white.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No visible saturated chromatic noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}High overall noise density.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Medium-to-high luminance contrast.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Tiny particles and irregular horizontal segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short-to-medium horizontal structures with very small vertical height.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Slight horizontal orientation bias.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Continuous coverage without large empty regions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The output should resemble an unstable monochrome analog television signal or full-frame signal loss.\
Keep the RGB channels equal for generated monochrome noise:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 R = G = B = Luma
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2 \
Do not introduce RGB channel separation, colored chroma interference, rainbow streaks, or color bleeding.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Secondary Component \'97 Horizontal Luma Streak & Dropout Modulation\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a separate controllable process for horizontal streaks.\
This component must produce:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Short white horizontal interruptions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Longer horizontal streaks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dark and light horizontal smears.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Irregular horizontal extensions of existing noise structures.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Soft gray horizontal regions mixed with sharper white segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Variable streak lengths and local luminance intensity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The effect must operate on luminance only.\
Do not implement this as chromatic smear or broad geometric image displacement. It is a horizontal luminance-domain operation.\
The streak system should be independently adjustable without changing the basic static density.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Important Temporal Transition \'97 Fine Static to Long Horizontal Streaks\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 This is the most distinctive feature of the reference and must not be overlooked.\
The observed reference behavior is:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}00:00.000\'9600:00.500:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  Dense, fine-grained monochrome static with tiny particles and short horizontal segments.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}00:00.750:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  A noticeable structural change, with longer horizontal white streaks, smoother gray regions, and more visible horizontal luminance smearing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct this behavior through a temporal modulation system.\
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Introduce a controllable 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 Streak Evolution
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  parameter.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Allow streak length and horizontal smear strength to evolve independently of base static intensity.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Allow fine-grain density to decrease relatively as longer streaks become more prominent.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Preserve full-frame coverage throughout the transition.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Maintain the monochrome palette.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Avoid sudden artificial cuts unless explicitly selected by the user.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not hardcode the transition to 00:00.750. The reference is short, and its timing is only an observed example.\
Instead, expose a flexible temporal evolution mechanism with:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Automatic procedural evolution.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Manual/keyframed control where supported by the existing architecture.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frozen/static mode.\
{\listtext	\'95	}User-controlled evolution speed and seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The automatic mode should reproduce the observed progression as a tunable behavior, not force every render to follow one fixed timeline.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Procedural Generation and Algorithm\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use a deterministic hash-based or equivalent fast procedural generator.\
Generate luminance values using spatial and temporal coordinates, for example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Segment index along X.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Pixel or row position along Y.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal seed.\
{\listtext	\'95	}User seed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The generation process should support:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Fine-grained monochrome noise.\
{\listtext	2.	}Irregular horizontal segment lengths.\
{\listtext	3.	}Local brightness and contrast variation.\
{\listtext	4.	}Horizontal streak formation.\
{\listtext	5.	}White and dark dropout segments.\
{\listtext	6.	}Temporal transition between fine static and longer streak structures.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use separate random streams or decorrelated hash inputs for base static and streak modulation so changing streak parameters does not unnecessarily regenerate the entire noise distribution.\
Ensure the pattern is deterministic for the same input, seed, and frame time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Adjustable Parameters\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Provide functional controls:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Monochrome Static Intensity
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 overall noise strength.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	2.	}Horizontal Segment Length
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the length of generated horizontal noise structures.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	3.	}Static Density
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the density of fine particles and segments.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	4.	}Contrast
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the separation between dark and bright noise.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	5.	}Horizontal Streak Amount
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the strength and prevalence of horizontal streaks.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	6.	}Horizontal Streak Length
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls their maximum horizontal extension.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	7.	}Luma Smear
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls horizontal luminance spreading and softness.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	8.	}Streak Evolution
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the transition from fine static to longer streaks.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	9.	}Evolution Speed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls temporal evolution speed.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	10.	}Input Blend
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls the contribution of original footage.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	11.	}Animate With Time
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 enables or freezes temporal changes.\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	12.	}Random Seed
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  \'97 controls procedural variation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Avoid duplicated controls if existing VHSart parameters already provide the same functionality.\
Each parameter must produce a meaningful and independently testable visual change.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 7. Input and Output Modes\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Support:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Generated Monochrome Signal
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Generate a full-frame monochrome static output.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Allow the static to completely replace the original image.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Preserve consistent full-frame coverage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Blend With Input
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Composite monochrome static over the original footage.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Allow adjustment between the generated noise and original footage.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Keep Input Blend independent from noise intensity and streak strength.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not use the original image as a source of unwanted color variation in monochrome mode.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

